Cannon Mali-G57 hardware workaround
==================================

valhall-1691526.wa is copied byte-for-byte from the working reference tree:
MT6853T_xiaomi_custom_kernel/firmware/valhall-1691526.wa

Size: 440 bytes
SHA256: 1a52a7f3c7c8b15e13e226d0956091621a83baafd80a3f93debb8271110e5951

The reference arch/arm64/configs/cannon_defconfig already uses:
CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE="valhall-1691526.wa"
CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE_DIR="firmware"

Cannon's 6.12 config uses the same built-in firmware mechanism. This makes
the workaround available both before and after Android switches its rootfs,
without modifying the stock vendor partition or bypassing the GPU erratum.
The r32p1 JM loader expects the WA signature 0x4157 and format version 2.

Novatek NT36672A touch firmware
==============================
novatek_ts_fw.bin and novatek_ts_mp.bin are converted with objcopy -I ihex
-O binary from the working 4.14 reference firmware/*.bin.ihex files.
Each is 118784 bytes. Both match byte-for-byte ranges in the known-working
MIUI14 4.14 boot kernel (boot SHA256
8bf3c2169c5eb77974068fdd286918454f7bfba207ecd01c436bf1d94c95eabb).
Normal firmware starts at decompressed kernel offset 19952288, MP at 20071072.
Both carry firmware version 18, matching the live Rec2 /proc/nvt_fw_version.

Normal SHA256: 1f5f956304fcf214543648b2178732fdcba7d1cf39ef36c45834004be3743b75
MP SHA256: 19ee2abd9405e9d053153e4124eeee9359ec0fa1be1f31ea7c13bff1cc2cf19f

These are built in through CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE, available during module
probing before vendor mounts and after switch_root. Do not rename unrelated
firmware files to these names or infer the IC from candidate DTBO nodes.
